Value to compute: dfrac{11}{18} + dfrac{7}{-27}

Calculation:

dfrac{11}{18} + dfrac{7}{-27}

⇒ dfrac{11}{18} + dfrac{-7}{27}

⇒dfrac{11 times 3 - 7 times 2}{54} 

⇒ dfrac{33 - 14}{54} 

⇒ dfrac{19}{54} 

∴ The correct answer is option (2).

**Given:**

Selling Price (SP 1) = ₹18,700

Loss = 15%

**Formula used:**

Cost Price (CP) = dfrac{SP times 100}{100 - {Loss%}}

New Selling Price (SP 2) = dfrac{CP times (100 + {Gain%})}{100}

**Calculations:**

CP = dfrac{18700 times 100}{100 - 15}

⇒ CP = dfrac{18700 times 100}{85}

⇒ CP = ₹22,000

⇒ SP 2 = dfrac{22000 times (100 + 15)}{100}

⇒ SP 2 = dfrac{22000 times 115}{100} 

⇒ SP 2 = ₹25,300

**∴ The correct answer is option (4).**

